    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **44 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors. BUILD SUCCESS.**\n\n## Summary\n\nI updated the locality derivation in `Owner.java` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`) to prefer the postcode.\n\n`getLocality()` now:\n1. **Looks up the region by postcode range first** \u2014 via a new `regionForPostcode()` helper that scans `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES` (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) for the range containing the owner's 4-digit postcode.\n2. **Falls back to the city-to-region table** (`CITY_REGION`, default `\"UNKNOWN\"`) only when the postcode is absent, malformed, or in no known range.\n\nThis reuses the existing `REGION_POSTCODE_RANGES` table (the source of truth already used by postcode validation), so known cities with matching postcodes return the same region, while cities that share a name are disambiguated by their postcode. For example, an unknown city with postcode `3000` now correctly yields `VIC`.\n\nBoth the pre-existing locality test (Cp17: known-city and unknown-city fallback with no postcode) and the new postcode-precedence test (Cp30) pass, along with the whole suite.",
