    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered sequence for `POST /api/owners`, from the code as it stands. The request lands on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (V2 has no create endpoint), which implements the generated `OwnersApi` interface.\n\n## Before the controller body runs\n\n1. **Security / authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:110`). When `petclinic.security.enable=true`, the caller must be authenticated and hold `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, else 401/403.\n2. **Declarative Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` on the generated `OwnersApi.addOwner`. Constraints live on `OwnerFieldsDto`, checked before your code runs (failures \u2192 400 via `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$\")`\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,30)`, `@Pattern(\"^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$\")`\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)` (note: no E.164 pattern here)\n   - `email`: `@Size(1,255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode`: `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n   - `registrationDate`: `@Valid`\n\n## Inside `addOwner` \u2014 in execution order\n\n**Validations (each returns immediately on failure):**\n\n3. **Telephone normalization** (`:113`) \u2014 `normalizeTelephone(...)`; if it returns `null` \u2192 **400**.\n4. **Address normalization** (`:117`) \u2014 `Owner.normalizeAddress(...)`; if `null` or blank \u2192 **400**.\n5. **Map DTO \u2192 entity** (`:121`, `ownerMapper.toOwner`) then set the normalized telephone (`:122`). *(As a side note, `Owner`'s own setters normalize: `setAddress` trims/collapses/uppercases/expands abbreviations; `setEmail` lower-cases.)*\n6. **Postcode-vs-city check** (`:123`) \u2014 `owner.isPostcodeValidForCity()`; if false \u2192 **400**.\n7. **Duplicate / identity-key check** (`:133\u2013136`) \u2014 builds `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`, household segment still empty here) and scans **all** owners (`findAllOwners()`); any exact match \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n8. **Per-city cap** (`:138`) \u2014 `countOwnersInCity(city) >= 50` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT**.\n9. **Per-day registration cap** (`:141\u2013146`) \u2014 takes `registrationDate` (or `now()`), rolls it to a business day via `toBusinessDay`, then `countOwnersRegisteredOn(day) >= 100` \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS**.\n\n**Side-effects / field assignments (on success path):**\n\n10. **Bulk-signup warning flag** (`:148`) \u2014 `bulkSignupWarning = ownersRegisteredToday > 80`.\n11. **Household member lookup** (`:150`) \u2014 `findHouseholdMembers(lastName, normalizedAddress)`.\n12. Assigns onto the new owner (`:153\u2013156`):\n    - `registrationDate` (business-day-adjusted)\n    - `customerCode` = `nextCustomerCode(city, lastName)` (format `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`)\n    - `namesakeCount` = `countNamesakes(firstName, lastName)`\n    - `bulkSignupWarning`\n13. **Household linkage** (`:157\u2013166`) \u2014 only if `sharesHousehold == true` **and** members exist:\n    - compute SHA-256 `householdId`, set it on the new owner, set `householdSize = members + 1`\n    - **back-fill DB write on OTHER rows**: for each existing member lacking a household id, set it and `clinicService.saveOwner(member)` (separate transaction each).\n14. **Persist the new owner** (`:168`) \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `@Transactional`, `ownerRepository.save(...)` (JPA `persist` for a new id). Note `addOwner` itself is **not** `@Transactional`, so the member back-fills and the main save are independent transactions.\n15. **Audit log side-effect** (`:169`) \u2014 writes an `AUDIT` logger line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel.\n16. **Response** (`:171\u2013174`) \u2014 map back to `OwnerDto`, set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 CREATED**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **No entity lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist`/`@EntityListeners`), **no application events**, and **no custom `ConstraintValidator` for Owner** (the only one, `PetAgeValidator`, is for pets).\n- The strict client-facing field validation is on the **DTO**, not the `Owner` entity. The entity's own constraints (`@NotEmpty`, telephone `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")`, postcode `@Pattern`, `@Email`) are not re-triggered on the mapped entity in this flow \u2014 the equivalent checks happen imperatively (steps 3\u20136).\n- Every count/duplicate check (steps 7\u20139, plus `nextCustomerCode` and `countNamesakes`) reads the **entire owner table** at request time via `findAllOwners()`."
